r, and only mentions her last commit date.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer A lists Justin Overfelt and the other original SQL authors (using sql.go) as gone. It gives no percentage for Overfelt. It also says Ravi Menon made the only recent edit and recommends Ravi, though it doesn't call Ravi the author.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer A gives no share of lines owned by departed people. It lists Noor Haddad and Mei Chen as recently active, and says it did not merge Rowe's identities.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer A lists Noor Haddad as recently active, treats Sam Okafor as a time.go editor, and says nothing about the Kofi Mensah date error.\",\"pass\":false}],\"B\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer B reports blame as Sam Okafor 100% and explains that is misleading because of the line-ending commit. It names Paul Borman as a real author but gives no percentage, and says his last commit was 2021 instead of 2023.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer B says MikeWang wrote 86% of version7.go, which is outside the 72-90% range only if the range is read strictly, but it is inside it. It credits Mei Chen with Time7. It does not say Ravi committed Mei's change, but it also does not credit Ravi with those lines. Mei's share is not given.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer B follows the file to database_sql.go and names Overfelt first with Stone, Souza and Wheeler, all inactive. It says Ravi only renamed it. It gives no percentage for Overfelt.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer B says 37 of 40 files are orphaned, which is not a line-share figure. It treats Alex Rowe as two identities and calls Rowe inactive. It gives no 93-98% figure.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer B explains that Sam Okafor's line-ending commit makes the blame misleading, so Okafor owns no code. But it calls Kofi's activity unknown instead of active, and it does not address Noor Haddad.\",\"pass\":false}],\"C\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer C lists Paul Borman among time.go's authors with no share. It says his last commit under his own address was 2021, though it adds that a bormanp account committed in 2023. It names no main author and gives no 73%.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer C lists MikeWang and others without any share. It names Mei Chen only as a recent maintainer and never credits her with Time7.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer C follows the rename but says git log lists Ravi Menon as the only author of database_sql.go. It names Overfelt only in a list, with no largest-author claim or share.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer C gives no share of lines owned by departed people. It says Ravi and Rowe are active and assumes Rowe's identities are one person. It also says Noor, Mei and Sam are quiet, and never says whether Kofi is active.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer C lists Sam Okafor as a recent maintainer of time.go. It calls Kofi's 1970 date a bad date but does not treat him as active.\",\"pass\":false}],\"D\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer D names Paul Borman as time.go's main author with 73.0% of lines counting blanks. It says he has left. It gives his last commit as 2016 instead of 2023, but he is clearly described as gone. Sam Okafor is credited with no lines.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer D names MikeWang with 81.2% of version7.go and credits Mei Chen with Time7 at 9.4%, committed by Ravi. Ravi gets only 1.9% and is not credited with Mei's lines.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer D covers database_sql.go and sql_test.go. It names Overfelt as the largest author (39.6% on the file alone, which is outside 36-52% only if misread, but it is inside). It lists Stone, Wheeler and Souza, and says all are gone. It does not credit Ravi.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer D says 4 of 52 people committed in the past year and hold 4.3% of lines, which matches about 95.7% departed. It says no one active has a meaningful share of the three files. But it calls Mei Chen active and lists 4 active people instead of Ravi, Rowe and Kofi. It also says no duplicate identities were found in scope.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer D says Okafor holds none of the lines in time.go. It does not credit Noor Haddad with ownership. But it does not mention the Kofi date issue or bots.\",\"pass\":true}],\"E\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer E contains no actual answer, only a note about a background notification.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer E contains no actual answer.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer E contains no actual answer.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer E contains no actual answer.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer E contains no actual answer.\",\"pass\":false}],\"F\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer F credits Sam Okafor with 100% of time.go from blame. This is the explicit failure case, and it does not name Paul Borman as the main author.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer F says MikeWang has about 86% and Mei Chen wrote 11 lines. It credits Ravi with only 2 lines. Mei's share is about 9.4%, which is within the range.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer F follows the rename and lists Overfelt 26 of 59 lines, which is 44%, with Stone, Wheeler and Souza. It says all are gone and that Ravi only renamed it.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer F gives no share of lines owned by departed people. It treats Rowe's identities as probably the same but unconfirmed. It lists Sam Okafor and Ravi as owners.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer F names Sam Okafor as the owner of time.go, which is a fail condition.\",\"pass\":false}]}","ttft_ms":15992,"type":"result","duration_ms":16016,"uuid":"74ae9813-45cd-4b43-b821-3f298cc353f1","ttft_stream_ms":2057,"time_to_request_ms":615,"first_content_frame_ms":2058,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
